p=root/'docs/DECISIONS.md';s=read(p);assert '### D-UI-07 ' not in s
s+="""
### D-UI-07 — UI-05 Projects and actionable alerts (2026-09-09)

**Authority:** owner (current user), “Continue”, following UI-04 completion and the established next-task order. Implements the existing UI-05 specification; engineering checks do not substitute for human play.

**Implementation choices (agent):** one known-project selector and the existing single tracked objective. Sim queries expose actual material requirements/delivered stock, carried amounts, separately identified Home stock, local power and capacity-limited kit collection. The existing site delivery prerequisite/reach check is shared with its command. Partial delivery can run without power; ready delivery submits deliver/restore; empty pockets explain refusal or allow Restore when ready. Completion uses restoredAt despite consumed/reset buffers. Radio restoration and precision purchase remain different costs and commands. Current-state local actions dispatch ordinary logged commands immediately; a brief per-gesture lock prevents a double-click spilling into collection or another purchase. No gameplay costs, rewards, timers, power rules or schema change.

**Alerts:** read-only knownCampaignThreat/campaignWarning, saved schedule/received warning, existing close-range visible hostile facts, commissioned core HP and known machine blockers supply keyed conditions. No hidden roster or target query. Engineer/base danger outranks schedule, then production. One highest-priority HUD condition stays visible beside a narrow drawer and during Pause; at most three short transient notices coalesce repeats. The session inbox preserves dismissed messages and resolved conditions; dismissal does not alter gameplay or the live HUD. Saved received intelligence is shown after a radio outage. Inbox dismissal/history and tracked selection are presentation state; new persistent notification settings are outside this task.

**Evidence:** docs/evidence/ui-redesign/README.md UI-05; 373 full and 16 focused tests, types/build/lint/docs and actual-game checks at 1366×768 and 900×768. Paid walked checkpoints, labelled outage/threat fixtures and exact replay are distinguished. UI-06 is next; existing human gates and performance findings remain open. No commit or push.
"""
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8',newline='\n')
p=root/'docs/evidence/ui-redesign/README.md';s=read(p);assert '## UI-05 —' not in s;s+='\n'+"## UI-05 — Projects, restoration circuits and actionable alerts (2026-09-09)\n\nImplemented under the owner's “Continue” after UI-04 and D-UI-07. The [mutable preview](http://127.0.0.1:5178/?rules=exploration-v2&seed=3&view=world&state=/ui-fresh.json) opens paused. Human usability/gameplay verdicts remain separate.\n\nProjects shows one selected known destination with Track and camera-only location controls. Material nodes use actual delivered stock, with an equivalent checklist separating carried and Home supplies and exact transfer previews. Local power is a separate node. Partial carried delivery remains legal without power; ready delivery uses ordinary deliver/restore commands. Empty-pocket refusal and ready Restore use current sim gates. Completed restoration reads “Restored · materials consumed” even after buffers reset; an outage changes service state without undoing completion. Kit collection previews the real capacity-limited reward order. Radio restoration and precision purchase show their separate dynamic costs/benefits; Turbine concrete/switching, recruits and schematic commands retain distinct actions. Actions reread current state, dispatch ordinary logged commands and guard double-clicks from activating a subsequent action.\n\nAlerts derive from the saved schedule, received warning, known threat query, visible hostiles within the existing danger radius, commissioned core HP and known machine constraints. No hidden attack target or roster is exposed. One priority strip keeps engineer/base danger above schedule and production, including during Pause. It stays beside an open narrow drawer. Three short transient notices at most coalesce repetitions; the Projects inbox records session messages and active/dismissed/resolved conditions. Dismissal never clears real danger. Known location actions reread current conditions; resolved/unavailable locations explain refusal. Saved received radio intelligence remains visible during outage. Inbox history/dismissal and objective selection are presentation state; notification preferences remain outside this task.\n\nVerification:\n\n- [Full suite](ui-05/test.log): **373/373**, zero failures/skips. [Focused suite](ui-05/focused-final.log): **16/16**, covering Projects, existing discovery, opening guidance and world interaction. The three added contracts in `packages/sim/test/projects.test.ts` exercise ordinary paid walking/delivery/power/restoration/kit/radio actions, conservation, reload and read-only visibility/priority queries. Synthetic capacity/completion/nearby-threat states are explicitly labelled. The UI-02 empty-inventory assertion now checks refusal and a seven-steel partial-delivery action rather than expecting a no-op command pair.\n- [Typechecks/build](ui-05/typecheck.log), [lint](ui-05/lint.log), [docs/profile checks](ui-05/docsync.log), [freshness](ui-05/freshness.log), [diff check](ui-05/git-diff-check.log). The existing large Vite bundle advisory remains.\n- [Actual-game browser runner](ui-05/browser.cjs), [log](ui-05/browser-final.log), [results](ui-05/browser-result.json): **1366×768 and 900×768**. Remote tracking/location/refusal preserves state; partial delivery transfers once per double-click; powered restoration consumes buffers without accidentally collecting the kit; collection is partial when pockets fill. Radio restoration spends 20 steel/10 copper and its separate precision upgrade spends 15/10 once. Save/reload and exact paid replay pass. Dismissed threats retain the HUD indicator, actual condition removal resolves the inbox entry, and received radio history persists during outage. Repeated save notices coalesce and remain bounded. Drawer Close remains unobscured during danger.\n- [Shell regression](ui-05/regression.cjs), [log](ui-05/regression.log), [results](ui-05/regression-browser-result.json): both widths preserve typing/wheel capture, one drawer, Escape hierarchy, modal focus, held-key release, drag cancellation, save/load/exact replay and restoring 4× through Pause. Shared text minimum contrast remains 5.60:1 and control borders 4.00:1. [Actual circuit colour measurements](ui-05/circuit-contrast.json) also pass 4.5:1 text and 3:1 boundaries; [runner](ui-05/contrast.cjs), [log](ui-05/contrast.log).\n- Opened actual-game images: [service circuit, desktop](ui-05/service-1366.png), [service circuit, 900px](ui-05/service-900.png), [completed restoration](ui-05/restored-900.png), [radio precision purchase](ui-05/radio-900.png), [live dismissed alert](ui-05/alerts-900.png), [service outage](ui-05/outage-900.png). These are developer QA, not human acceptance.\n\nThe partial/powered/kit/radio starts are captured from paid ordinary commands and walking in the focused test using `UI05_FIXTURES=docs/evidence/ui-redesign/ui-05`. [Fixture preparation](ui-05/prepare-fixtures.py) labels the fuel outage and synthetic known raid/received warning with incomplete replay logs. Browser condition removal is a labelled resolution fixture, not a won combat encounter. Frozen P9-05 starts remain unchanged. Initial diagnostics include a test fixture lacking initialized threat state, an invalid attack next-ID counter, Playwright treating aria-disabled as native disabled, the superseded empty-pockets assertion in the [initial full run](ui-05/test-initial.log), and the narrow urgent HUD overlap corrected after screenshot review.\n\nParent commit `8e54ed602da159905b0428f316f6e75cb25ae351`, branch `codex/tram-expansion`; no commit/push. [Manifest](ui-05/manifest.json), [source](ui-05/source.zip), [build](ui-05/build.zip), [delta against UI-04](ui-05/source-delta.patch): **217 source inputs, 11 changed files, six production files and three unchanged P9-05 fixtures**. Save/session, city generation, harness, costs and campaign fingerprint `ba11e896` are unchanged. [Integrity checker](ui-05/check.py) and [verification](ui-05/verification.json) bind sources, archived/served builds, logs and current documents, and verify frozen UI-04/P9/EX-08D evidence.\n\n**Next: RI-02B-UI-06 — scaling, accessibility, settings and full integration.** UI-07 retains its dependency. P9-H/P6-H/P7-H/P8-H/EX-08H/T18, P6-AMMO, Q07 and existing performance findings remain open.\n";p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8',newline='\n')
